+{
+  "tool": "built-in image_gen",
+  "reference_images": [],
+  "images": [
+    {
+      "file": "805-aerobics-video.png",
+      "prompt": "Generate a brand-new image from text only, without any reference images. One 1024x1024 square image. Authentic frame from a 1980s home aerobics VHS tape, with the entire staging, video medium and composition dictated by that era. Neon pink and electric teal exercise studio, mirrored wall, glossy reflective floor. A woman in her early 30s, large and prominent in frame, with shoulder-length bouncy curly auburn hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, terry headband and a big cheerful smile, mid side-stretch with a wide athletic stance. Full-body dynamic framing from a slightly low camera angle. She wears a high-cut mustard-yellow leotard over tights and chunky leg warmers; her mustard-yellow knit sweater is tied around her waist. One raised hand holds an upright coffee cup as she enjoys her coffee break while stretching. A croissant is nearby on a small plate on the studio bench. Period studio lighting and authentic analog video softness, interlaced softness, chroma color bleed, horizontal tracking noise near the lower edge, subtle warped VHS signal. It should look like an actual old exercise video frame, with period-authentic styling and camera blocking. No text of any kind, no captions, no timer, no logos, no signatures, no watermark."
+    },
+    {
+      "file": "806-untitled-goose-game.png",
+      "prompt": "Generate a brand-new image from text only, without any reference images. One 1024x1024 square image in the authentic visual look of Untitled Goose Game. Flat pastel 3D game environment, simple untextured geometric shapes, no outlines, minimal almost orthographic perspective from a gentle high angle, soft even lighting. An English village garden with a garden path, simple hedges, a little wooden gate and a modest garden table. The main character is a large prominent simple faceless adult woman villager representing a woman in her early 30s, shoulder-length curly auburn hair reduced to simple sculpted clumps, round tortoiseshell glasses, mustard-yellow sweater represented as a plain untextured color block, simplified skirt and shoes. Her blank face has no detailed facial features; the style takes priority over realistic anatomy or freckles. Full-body three-quarter rear/profile view as she twists toward a mischievous white goose. She holds her coffee cup upright in one hand while the goose steals her croissant and scampers away with it in its beak. Make the goose theft visually unambiguous. Distinct, playful diagonal action composition with generous garden space, authentic minimal stylized low-detail game rendering. No photographic textures, no realistic skin, no elaborate materials or dramatic lighting, no UI, no text, no captions, no logos, no signatures, no watermark."
+    },
+    {
+      "file": "807-cabbage-patch.png",
+      "prompt": "Generate a brand-new image from text only, without any reference images. One 1024x1024 square image. Authentic Cabbage Patch Kids doll photography with the visual language of an early 1980s toy-store catalog studio photograph. The doll is an interpretation of a woman in her early 30s, with the doll style completely determining anatomy and proportions: a broad soft-sculpture molded vinyl face with plump round cheeks, small close-set eyes, little nose and tiny sweet smile; freckles painted on the cheeks, shoulder-length thick curly auburn yarn hair, tiny round tortoiseshell glasses and a chunky mustard-yellow knit sweater. Soft stuffed cloth body, short chubby fabric arms and legs. The entire seated doll is large in frame, posed with feet forward on a softly draped pale peach studio backdrop, a very tactile handmade toy with yarn loops, molded vinyl and cloth seams. She holds a toy coffee cup in her cloth hands, and a little toy croissant on a plate sits immediately beside her. Straight-on slightly elevated catalog composition, warm soft studio fill, gentle aged color-print rendering, period toy-shop photography. The result must unmistakably look like a physical Cabbage Patch doll, not a human portrait and not a giant-eyed fashion doll. No packaging, no text of any kind, no labels, no captions, no signatures, no logos, no watermark."
+    },
+    {
+      "file": "808-blythe-doll.png",
+      "prompt": "Generate a brand-new image from text only, without any reference images. One 1024x1024 square image. Authentic photograph of a custom Blythe doll in a miniature cafe set, with an oversized head, very huge glassy color-changing doll eyes showing luminous green irises, and an extremely tiny delicate body. This is a custom physical doll interpretation of a woman in her early 30s with shoulder-length curly auburn hair, hand-painted freckles, tiny round tortoiseshell glasses sized to her doll face, mustard-yellow miniature knit sweater. Beautifully carved and hand-painted face-up, subtle blush and small carved lips. Dreamy intimate close-up with her enormous head dominating the upper frame, an asymmetrical three-quarter profile turned toward soft window light, eyes gazing slightly sideways. Her tiny hands hold a miniature coffee cup and a miniature croissant close to her chest, both clearly visible. Cafe tabletop in foreground and miniature cafe furnishings melting into creamy shallow-depth-of-field bokeh. Realistic doll vinyl, carefully rooted synthetic curls, miniature knitted stitches, glass eyes and intricate tiny food props. Delicate soft window light with muted cafe colors, distinctly different composition from a full-body toy catalog photograph. It must look like a real custom Blythe collectible doll, not a human portrait. No text of any kind, no menu lettering, no captions, no logos, no signature, no watermark."
+    }
+  ]
+}

